The baseline and intermediate output files remain for comparison. Earlier successful full/filter checks are retained too.

Limits / deliberately untouched
Only live capture IO moved: initial ring admission still validates/opens the private directory on the supervisor actor. Public Client/Logic APIs, wire actions, R1 runtime ownership, adapters and consumer-side R3 code are unchanged. Media faults remain explicit IO failures; recovery from disk-full/device failure and strict power-cut/F_FULLFSYNC ordering were not tested. A bounded full queue can backpressure a writer; both 128 MiB acceptance modes recorded zero full episodes. No total cold quota is introduced. Supervisor death can discard queued/uncommitted data and still kills its PTYs; logic death while the supervisor lives does not.
No 1000-seat, multi-minute, noncompressible-data, real harness, UI/render, macOS14/Linux or hosted-CI performance claim. The 128 MiB test checks tail/no-gap/PID; complete bytewise history hashing is the separate 20 MiB test. Retained cold descriptors still grow with history.
Shared peer UI/lab work remains untouched. Sync attempts: git pull --ff-only (and per-call pull.rebase=false variant) refused unstaged shared edits; fetch succeeded, merge --ff-only later returned exit 128 (w1-2c-sync.log) while shared refs changed. No stash, reset, rebase, conflict resolution or non-FF merge was performed. Final signed SHA/scope are in the ICQ handoff.
